### ClaimDailyRewardV1 — runnable request collection
#
# Six requests covering the full contract. Run them top to bottom against a local host.
#
#   1. cd src/GameBackend && func start
#   2. Open this file and click "Send Request" above any block.
#
# Executes in Visual Studio 2022 (17.8+, built in), JetBrains Rider/IntelliJ (built in),
# or VS Code with the REST Client extension:  code --install-extension humao.rest-client
#
# State is a process-local singleton, so restarting the host resets every balance and
# claim. Run these twice without restarting and request 1 returns alreadyClaimed.
#
# NO FUNCTION KEY IS PRESENT OR NEEDED. Locally the host disables authorization
# regardless of authLevel. For the deployed variant, see the note at the end of the file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071
@contentType = application/json

### 1 — First claim of the UTC day grants 50
# Expect 200: rewardAmount 50, newlyClaimed true, alreadyClaimed false, balance 50,
# and playerEntityId "title_player_123" — the authenticated entity, NOT the
# clientPlayerId sent below, which the service binds but never reads.

# @name firstClaim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "FunctionArgument": {
    "questId": "daily_login",
    "clientRequestId": "request-001",
    "clientPlayerId": "do-not-trust-this-field"
  },
  "CallerEntityProfile": {
    "Entity": { "Id": "title_player_123", "Type": "title_player_account" }
  }
}

### 2 — Identical request again is idempotent
# Expect 200: rewardAmount 0, alreadyClaimed true, balance unchanged, success still true.
# A duplicate is a successful no-op rather than an error, so a retrying client does not
# escalate. The balance returned is the player's real balance, for client reconciliation.

# @name duplicateClaim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "FunctionArgument": {
    "questId": "daily_login",
    "clientRequestId": "request-001",
    "clientPlayerId": "do-not-trust-this-field"
  },
  "CallerEntityProfile": {
    "Entity": { "Id": "title_player_123", "Type": "title_player_account" }
  }
}

### 3 — A different clientRequestId does not re-grant
# Expect 200: alreadyClaimed true, rewardAmount 0.
# Deduplication keys on daily_login:{entityId}:{server UTC date} — every component is
# server-derived. clientRequestId is client-controlled and is used for tracing only, so
# varying it cannot produce a second grant.

# @name variedClientRequestId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "FunctionArgument": {
    "questId": "daily_login",
    "clientRequestId": "a-completely-different-id"
  },
  "CallerEntityProfile": {
    "Entity": { "Id": "title_player_123", "Type": "title_player_account" }
  }
}

### 4 — Missing caller entity is rejected
# Expect 400: errorCode "MissingCallerEntity", success false.
# The request carries a well-formed clientPlayerId and is still refused: there is no
# path from client-controlled data to a grant.

# @name missingCallerEntity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "FunctionArgument": {
    "questId": "daily_login",
    "clientPlayerId": "title_player_123"
  }
}

### 5 — Unknown quest is rejected without mutation
# Expect 400: errorCode "UnknownQuest".
# The allow-list is checked before any dependency is touched, so a bad quest id cannot
# consume that player's daily claim. Re-run request 1 with this player id to confirm
# nothing was recorded.

# @name unknownQuest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "FunctionArgument": { "questId": "weekly_login" },
  "CallerEntityProfile": {
    "Entity": { "Id": "title_player_999", "Type": "title_player_account" }
  }
}

### 6 — Malformed body returns 400, not 500
# Expect 400: errorCode "BadRequest".
# JsonException is caught and folded into the same path as an absent body. A 500 here
# would leak framework internals and signal to a caller that the parser failed.

# @name malformedBody
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

this is not json at all

###

# Against a deployed Function App the authLevel is enforced and a function key is required.
# Read it from the environment so it never enters this file, and send it as a header rather
# than ?code= — query strings land in server access logs. Use a function-scoped key.
#
#   POST https://<app-name>.azurewebsites.net/api/ClaimDailyRewardV1 HTTP/1.1
#   Content-Type: {{contentType}}
#   x-functions-key: {{$processEnv CURLYBLUE_FUNCTION_KEY}}
